S8 Mali PA-panic fix (0138): buffers are wired kmem_alloc pages (the 0130 self-test recipe) described by a plain kernel-task
IOGeneralMemoryDescriptor subclass (S8MaliBO) instead of an IOBufferMemoryDescriptor with kIOMapWriteCombineCache; PAs come
from pmap_find_phys only (checked against the managed RAM range); the program's mapping is the default cacheable one and every
buffer is cleaned+invalidated by kernel VA before and after each job. Boot-arg s8mali_trace=1 prints the first 200 steps (each
before the call it names). Also pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys used (pp << PAGE_SHIFT) on a 32 bit ppnum_t (lost bits 32+ of the
PA, RAM is at 0x880000000): now ptoa(pp).

